<v Nick Flynn>Four years ago.
<v Nick Flynn>四年前。

00:53:15.700 --> 00:53:23.900
<v Nick's Father>How the hell you'd go to the NYU [UNINTELLIGIBLE] school? I don't know what promoted you. How'd you go there? You majored in writing?
<v Nick's Father>你怎么进纽约大学[听不清]学校的？我不知道是什么提拔了你。你怎么去那里的？你是主修写作的？

00:53:23.900 --> 00:53:25.310
<v Nick Flynn>Yeah.
<v Nick Flynn>是的。

00:53:25.310 --> 00:53:37.130
<v Nick's Father>Struggling fully. He knows how successful his father is as a writer.
<v Nick's Father>他完全是个挣扎者。他知道他的父亲作为一名作家有多成功。

00:53:37.130 --> 00:54:11.710
<v Nick Flynn>A lot of times I'm very frustrated when I go and meet with him because it seems like he tells the same stories over and over again. They seem very disconnected to reality. But those few times where I have felt some connection, it does seem that he's just let his guard down a little bit and let me glimpse at his struggle in some way. You know, what connects us. He actually wrote me a letter right after-- he sent me a couple letters after my book of poems came out.
<v Nick Flynn>很多时候我去找他见面都会感到非常沮丧，因为他似乎总是重复说同样的故事。他们似乎与现实完全脱节。但有几次我觉得有一些联系，似乎他确实放下了防备，让我瞥见了他的挣扎。你知道，是什么联系着我们。其实他确实给我写了一封信——我的诗集出来后他寄了两封信给我。

00:54:11.710 --> 00:54:38.300
<v Nick Flynn>In the first one it just says, "Dear Nick, your book is a classic. Love, your father." That's a unique letter. Because the classic has only been a word that he's ever reserved for his own work. And so for him to apply that to my is just sort of him turning, even if just for a second and sort of looking at me and saying something about what I've done.
<v Nick Flynn>第一封信上写着，“亲爱的尼克，你的书是一部经典。爱你的，父亲。”那是一封独特的信。因为“经典”这个词是他一直只保留给自己作品的词。所以他把它用在我的书上，只是他的一种转变，即使只是一瞬间，他转过身看着我说了一些关于我做的事情的话。

00:54:38.300 --> 00:54:58.970
<v Nick Flynn>There has to be a reason that I've held onto his letters for all these years. There has to be some sort of reason, something I've been waiting for, or looking for, or hoping for. And yes, something like this is sort of maybe as close as I'll get to it.
<v Nick Flynn>我这么多年来一直留着他的信肯定是有原因的。一定有某种理由，我在等待、寻找或希望得到什么。是的，像这样的一点点，也许就是我能得到的接近了。

00:54:58.970 --> 00:55:36.630
<v Nick Flynn>I would like to have sort of one of those deep, connecting moments with him. But I'm not really sure if I've achieved that yet. Again, I'm actually not even sure if at this point, I would hope for or-- sure. Maybe you always hope for it, you just sort of deny that hope or something. I don't know if I even hope for it at this point. It's almost enough just to sit in front of him. To go to his room and sit with him for an hour. And just see where he is. And tell him, whatever. I'll tell him one thing about myself. If he hears it, that's great. If he doesn't hear it, that's fine.
<v Nick Flynn>我希望能和他有那种深刻的联系时刻。但我真的不确定我是否已经达到了。再说一次，我甚至不确定在这一点上，我是会希望还是——确定。也许你总是希望得到它，你只是否认那种希望什么的。我不知道我在这点上是否还抱有希望。光是坐在他面前就足够了。去他的房间坐一个小时。看看他在哪。告诉他，随便什么。告诉他一件关于我自己的事。如果他听进去了，那太好了。如果他没听见，也没关系。

00:55:36.630 --> 00:56:13.740
<v Nick Flynn>I don't expect him to give me anything at this point. It's almost enough just to go and see him. It somehow calms me enough or settles my soul enough just to go and have some relationship at all with him. I'm sort of down to the real basic, like really stripped down to the most basic father there can be. He just is my father and there's nothing I can do about that. There's nothing he can do about that. I go and I sit and I have a relationship with this person who is my father.
<v Nick Flynn>我没指望他现在能给我什么。光是去看他就够了。光是建立哪怕一点点关系，在某种程度上就足够让我平静或安抚我的灵魂。我基本已经降到了最基本的程度，真的很剥离到了父亲最基本的状态。他就是我父亲，对此我无能为力。他也无能为力。我去坐着，和他这个是我父亲的人保持着一种关系。

00:56:13.740 --> 00:56:23.500
<v Ira Glass>Nick Flynn's book of poems is called Some Ether . He's working on a book in which his dad figures prominently.
<v Ira Glass>尼克·弗林的诗集名为《某种醚》。他正在写一本书，他父亲在其中占有重要地位。

